1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:01,067
Love...

2
00:00:01,167 --> 00:00:02,767
Impossible...

3
00:00:02,867 --> 00:00:04,433
That guy is my sister's boyfriend.

4
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,343
I heard you still can't bring
yourself to call him "So-chan"?

5
00:00:06,367 --> 00:00:07,533
Mom, where's Rock?

6
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:08,033
Not here.

7
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,443
- Huh?
- I can't find him anywhere.

8
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:10,167
Rock!

9
00:00:10,267 --> 00:00:13,400
Rock!

10
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,100
Are you okay?

11
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,400
Yeah.

12
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,167
If it weren't for So-chan...
things would've been really bad.

13
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:23,967
Here, this is for you.

14
00:00:24,767 --> 00:00:29,733
I like the things my sister likes...

15
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:40,100
"Your Summer, My Storm"
(Episode 4)

16
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,633
Does my sister report to you too, So-chan?

17
00:00:44,733 --> 00:00:49,167
Yeah, she just texted me saying,
"Okinawa steak is amazing."

18
00:00:49,267 --> 00:00:50,267
She really did.

19
00:00:51,567 --> 00:00:53,667
Our family only found out yesterday too.

20
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:54,600
I see.

21
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:55,700
Yeah.

22
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,300
I'm heading out!

23
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,333
- Oh, take care.
- But she's always been like this.

24
00:01:00,433 --> 00:01:04,433
But I actually admire that about Rio.

25
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:07,700
Huh? What's there to admire?

26
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:11,700
If I don't plan my
schedule days in advance,

27
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,367
I can't get anything done.

28
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:15,133
Being organized is a good thing.

29
00:01:15,233 --> 00:01:17,167
But doesn't that make me a boring person?

30
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:19,833
Not at all. You're very
interesting, So-chan.

31
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:21,309
You don't have to force
yourself to comfort me.

32
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:23,700
Just being a bridge nerd is weird enough.

33
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,320
I've never even heard of such a thing.

34
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,067
I see.

35
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:30,167
Yeah.

36
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:32,167
I'm actually kind of happy.

37
00:01:34,233 --> 00:01:38,133
"Weird" and "interesting"
aren't exactly compliments.

38
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:40,600
They are to me.

39
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,700
It's the first time anyone's
ever said that to me.

40
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:46,200
Oh, really?

41
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:47,633
What is going on?

42
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:51,067
This phenomenon where I find
him dazzling from time to time...

43
00:01:51,833 --> 00:01:53,067
It's love.

44
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:55,933
- Huh?
- In English, it's "Love."

45
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,767
Love? You sure have the
nerve to just say it out loud.

46
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:03,067
Only because you
asked so directly, Natsuki.

47
00:02:03,667 --> 00:02:06,267
It's because a friend of
mine is struggling with this.

48
00:02:06,367 --> 00:02:07,643
I want to help him figure it out.

49
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:11,067
So this friend of yours
hated the guy at first,

50
00:02:11,167 --> 00:02:14,000
but slowly started falling for him, right?

51
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:15,633
He didn't say he liked him.

52
00:02:15,733 --> 00:02:17,033
Oh.

53
00:02:18,733 --> 00:02:20,367
He just changed his mind about him.

54
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,433
He just doesn't hate him anymore.

55
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:23,533
That's exactly it!

56
00:02:23,633 --> 00:02:24,200
What?

57
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:25,409
At first, they couldn't stand each other.

58
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:26,909
Then they discover a cute side to them.

59
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:29,933
And now they're wondering
if they've fallen for them.

60
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:31,300
Oh my.

61
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,300
Stop squealing!

62
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,933
That's a classic teen manga trope!

63
00:02:34,033 --> 00:02:34,733
It's completely different, okay?

64
00:02:34,833 --> 00:02:36,500
How can you be so sure?

65
00:02:38,233 --> 00:02:41,700
Because it's someone
he could never fall for.

66
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,933
Huh, what kind of person are they?

67
00:02:48,067 --> 00:02:50,800
I heard it's his close friend's partner.

68
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,833
Stealing someone's lover?

69
00:02:52,933 --> 00:02:53,833
Or a forbidden romance?

70
00:02:53,933 --> 00:02:55,800
- What?
- Don't tell me... is it an affair?

71
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:57,100
Not at all.

72
00:02:59,133 --> 00:02:59,867
Hello.

73
00:02:59,967 --> 00:03:01,133
Oh, welcome.

74
00:03:01,233 --> 00:03:02,033
Please grab a seat anywhere.

75
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:02,733
Okay.

76
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:06,767
So lucky. I want to go to Okinawa too.

77
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:08,700
You should've just gone with them, Yui-san.

78
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:10,767
Seriously, get out of the way.

79
00:03:10,867 --> 00:03:11,900
Here you go.

80
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,400
What would you like to order?

81
00:03:15,159 --> 00:03:16,459
I'll have the yurinchi.

82
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,209
One order of yurinchi, coming right up.

83
00:03:18,233 --> 00:03:21,367
Ah, you're Natsuki's tutor.

84
00:03:21,633 --> 00:03:23,800
You're Na-chan's friend...

85
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:24,900
Kazu-kun?

86
00:03:24,967 --> 00:03:26,667
You came here with Rio a while ago, right?

87
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:27,300
Huh?

88
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,609
Are you the Sota-san
I've heard so much about?

89
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:30,500
Yes. Wait, heard so much about?

90
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,967
Rio talks about you all the time.

91
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:34,333
Rio and I have been
friends since middle school.

92
00:03:34,433 --> 00:03:34,967
I see.

93
00:03:35,067 --> 00:03:38,100
And I'm Natsuki's best friend.

94
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:40,867
And also Rio-san's junior.

95
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:42,667
Nice to meet you.

96
00:03:42,767 --> 00:03:42,933
Yeah.

97
00:03:43,033 --> 00:03:44,833
I'm Kagami Yui.

98
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:46,467
I didn't expect to run into you here.

99
00:03:46,567 --> 00:03:47,867
This is great.

100
00:03:47,967 --> 00:03:50,000
Let's take a picture. I
want to send it to Rio.

101
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,500
Okay, smile!

102
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:52,767
Don't jump in!

103
00:03:52,867 --> 00:03:53,667
Just take it.

104
00:03:53,767 --> 00:03:55,467
Come on, smile!

105
00:03:57,533 --> 00:04:04,500
Gravitation is not responsible
for people falling in love.

106
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,267
Albert Einstein.

107
00:04:06,367 --> 00:04:09,633
Gravitation... what even is that?

108
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:17,500
Speaking of which, what exactly is "love"?

109
00:04:20,033 --> 00:04:22,500
The feeling of affection
between a man and a woman.

110
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,200
Love.

111
00:04:24,633 --> 00:04:26,067
Love...

112
00:04:28,867 --> 00:04:30,033
(What is love?)

113
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:32,167
What?

114
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:35,933
A man and a woman having
affection for each other.

115
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:37,300
Love?

116
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:38,833
This is just going in circles.

117
00:04:38,933 --> 00:04:40,300
Natsuki.

118
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,100
Huh?

119
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,633
Riku.

120
00:04:43,433 --> 00:04:45,833
You can chat here, but no yelling.

121
00:04:45,933 --> 00:04:47,400
I know.

122
00:04:50,033 --> 00:04:51,043
I've been running into you a lot lately.

123
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:53,067
Natsuki, did you get
your heart broken again?

124
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,767
No, I didn't.

125
00:04:55,867 --> 00:04:57,667
Is your teacher not here today?

126
00:04:58,133 --> 00:04:59,467
Teacher?

127
00:04:59,567 --> 00:05:01,133
Oh, you mean So-chan.

128
00:05:01,233 --> 00:05:02,233
He's not here.

129
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,567
I actually had something
I wanted to ask him.

130
00:05:04,667 --> 00:05:05,233
Oh, really?

131
00:05:05,333 --> 00:05:06,167
I'll answer it for you then.

132
00:05:06,267 --> 00:05:06,800
Huh?

133
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,300
What's with that reaction?

134
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,267
I have way more life
experience than you do.

135
00:05:11,967 --> 00:05:12,967
What's with that look?

136
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,433
Sota-san.

137
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,800
I'm always on Rio's side.

138
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:20,300
Nice to meet you.

139
00:05:21,433 --> 00:05:24,000
You're so righteous and stern, it's impressive.

140
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:25,233
Speaking of how we met...

141
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:27,467
- So cool.
- It goes all the way back to kindergarten.

142
00:05:27,833 --> 00:05:30,033
So pretty.

143
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:34,233
You must think you're pretty cool, huh?

144
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:37,267
- No, I don't.
- Why are you acting so cocky?

145
00:05:42,667 --> 00:05:43,833
Hey!

146
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:45,900
What?

147
00:05:45,933 --> 00:05:48,433
Don't pick on my little brother.

148
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,000
So cool.

149
00:05:53,667 --> 00:05:58,400
From that day on, Rio-san has been my hero.

150
00:05:59,367 --> 00:06:00,400
What do you mean?

151
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,600
I see.

152
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,333
You have three people you like?

153
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,900
Yeah.

154
00:06:05,967 --> 00:06:08,767
Teacher Ayaka, Nono-chan,

155
00:06:08,867 --> 00:06:10,233
and Umi-kun.

156
00:06:10,333 --> 00:06:12,167
They're all very different types.

157
00:06:12,267 --> 00:06:14,733
I really like all three of them.

158
00:06:15,467 --> 00:06:17,100
I see.

159
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:23,467
What does it feel like
to "really like" someone?

160
00:06:23,567 --> 00:06:26,900
It's fun, and I want to keep
playing with them forever.

161
00:06:28,833 --> 00:06:30,400
I see.

162
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,800
Do I really have to choose just one?

163
00:06:34,933 --> 00:06:36,800
Well...

164
00:06:39,867 --> 00:06:42,900
I knew I couldn't count on Na-chan.

165
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:44,167
Huh?

166
00:06:44,267 --> 00:06:45,400
Bye-bye!

167
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:46,833
Hey, Riku!

168
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:51,300
So "liking" someone means feeling happy,

169
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:54,533
and wanting to stay by
their side forever... is that it?

170
00:06:56,667 --> 00:07:01,200
I definitely don't want
to stay by that guy's side forever.

171
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,900
Which means, I don't "like" him.

172
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,667
Exactly. This feeling isn't "love."

173
00:07:08,333 --> 00:07:10,400
Ah... I feel so much better.

174
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:25,300
That lightning strike
was super close, wasn't it?

175
00:07:26,267 --> 00:07:27,467
Yeah...

176
00:07:27,567 --> 00:07:30,800
There was a massive
cumulonimbus cloud earlier, after all.

177
00:07:35,667 --> 00:07:39,767
It's probably just a passing shower.

178
00:07:41,833 --> 00:07:44,500
So-chan, are you scared of thunder?

179
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,933
No, not at all.

180
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:48,600
Whoa!

181
00:07:58,833 --> 00:07:59,900
Are you okay?

182
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,833
I'm completely fine.

183
00:08:03,167 --> 00:08:04,167
Right.

184
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:07,167
- Whoa!
- Ah!

185
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:10,500
I'm fine.

186
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:14,800
Even if I occasionally
find him dazzling or cute,

187
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:16,133
it's all just an illusion.

188
00:08:16,233 --> 00:08:18,000
Give me a break.

189
00:08:20,633 --> 00:08:23,533
Fuku-chan, be careful not to catch a cold.

190
00:08:23,633 --> 00:08:26,600
Sorry, the trains are suspended.

191
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,409
(A relative living nearby, Mineta Fukuo)
There's a huge line at the bus stop too.

192
00:08:28,433 --> 00:08:30,967
Before I knew it, I had
walked all the way here.

193
00:08:31,067 --> 00:08:32,543
You should've just walked straight home.

194
00:08:32,567 --> 00:08:35,800
How could I pass by the old man's
house without dropping in?

195
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:37,467
You're going to eat with us, right?

196
00:08:37,567 --> 00:08:38,167
Is that okay?

197
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:39,000
Sure.

198
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:40,400
Seriously...

199
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,367
Oh, by the way...

200
00:08:43,467 --> 00:08:45,300
Is the teacher going to be okay?

201
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,300
Oh, right.

202
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,600
What teacher?

203
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:51,733
Ah, the trains are suspended...

204
00:08:52,667 --> 00:08:54,233
Huh?

205
00:08:54,333 --> 00:08:55,200
Are you kidding me...

206
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,633
This is bad...

207
00:09:04,167 --> 00:09:05,700
This is so good!

208
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,167
Really?

209
00:09:07,267 --> 00:09:09,733
Father made this soba.

210
00:09:09,833 --> 00:09:10,967
Wait, what?

211
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:14,500
It's not quite good enough
to serve to customers yet,

212
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,867
but I've been taking handmade soba classes.

213
00:09:16,967 --> 00:09:18,100
That's amazing.

214
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:19,400
It's delicious.

215
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:22,067
Yeah, you've got a
real talent for it, old man.

216
00:09:22,167 --> 00:09:24,067
I'd be completely hopeless at it.

217
00:09:24,167 --> 00:09:26,633
Fuku-chan, you just went
along with him at first, right?

218
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:28,093
I never asked him to come with me.

219
00:09:28,167 --> 00:09:30,300
It's true that I was the one
who said I wanted to go,

220
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:35,100
but I was mostly just looking forward to
grabbing a drink with the old man afterward.

221
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,033
I knew it.

222
00:09:37,133 --> 00:09:40,900
Father is a total workaholic
with zero hobbies.

223
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,667
If he kept working like that until
retirement, he'd be bored out of his mind.

224
00:09:44,767 --> 00:09:46,700
So I wanted to help him find a hobby.

225
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,967
You're already preparing for that?

226
00:09:49,067 --> 00:09:50,800
Well, the sooner, the better.

227
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:53,933
But the old man has another
reason for doing it, too.

228
00:09:54,033 --> 00:09:55,133
Fukuo.

229
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:56,033
Huh?

230
00:09:56,133 --> 00:09:58,267
What other reason?

231
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:01,367
You scared me!

232
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:02,267
Rock.

233
00:10:02,367 --> 00:10:03,667
Rock is right here.

234
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,900
Sota-san, there's plenty more, so eat up.

235
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,167
Thank you.

236
00:10:09,267 --> 00:10:10,376
Everything is absolutely delicious.

237
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:12,133
- I'm so glad you like it.
- Eat up.

238
00:10:12,233 --> 00:10:12,933
Thank you.

239
00:10:13,033 --> 00:10:14,700
- Have some more.
- Thanks.

240
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:17,733
By the way, So-chan,
what do you usually do for meals?

241
00:10:17,832 --> 00:10:19,866
Do you live alone?

242
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:22,200
Yes, I mostly cook for myself.

243
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,100
That's impressive!

244
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,367
But I only make really simple dishes.

245
00:10:25,467 --> 00:10:28,767
Hey, do you want to come to
our cooking class next time?

246
00:10:28,867 --> 00:10:30,800
Oh, is that okay?

247
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,767
Of course, we'd love to have you.

248
00:10:32,867 --> 00:10:34,376
It's always great to have a new member.

249
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,033
- Yeah.
- I'm looking forward to it.

250
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:37,600
You definitely have to come.

251
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:42,300
The trains still aren't running, right?

252
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:42,733
Yeah.

253
00:10:42,833 --> 00:10:44,833
But they should be back
up and running soon.

254
00:10:44,933 --> 00:10:48,500
I doubt the trains will
resume service tonight.

255
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,800
Really? You think so?

256
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,133
They haven't announced it yet,

257
00:10:53,233 --> 00:10:55,633
but until they can
confirm it's safe to run,

258
00:10:55,733 --> 00:10:58,000
it's probably going to take quite a while.

259
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:59,233
I see.

260
00:11:00,033 --> 00:11:01,700
I'll just walk back, then.

261
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:02,833
What?

262
00:11:02,933 --> 00:11:05,100
It'll take at least an hour
to walk back, won't it?

263
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:08,100
You can't do that, you'll catch a cold.

264
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,200
Or maybe...

265
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,433
How about you stay the night here?

266
00:11:11,533 --> 00:11:11,833
Huh?

267
00:11:11,933 --> 00:11:15,167
Yeah, Sota-san, let's do that.

268
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:16,267
There we go.

269
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:18,433
Wait, hold on.

270
00:11:18,533 --> 00:11:19,633
Thank you.

271
00:11:19,733 --> 00:11:22,233
Sota-san, you can sleep here tonight.

272
00:11:22,333 --> 00:11:24,013
Wait, I'm not sleeping in the living room?

273
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:28,067
Your dad gets up to use the bathroom in the
middle of the night. He wouldn't sleep well.

274
00:11:28,167 --> 00:11:29,367
It's better if he sleeps here.

275
00:11:29,433 --> 00:11:30,333
What do you mean, "better"?

276
00:11:30,433 --> 00:11:33,167
Hey, the bath is ready.

277
00:11:33,267 --> 00:11:34,667
Okay.

278
00:11:34,867 --> 00:11:37,167
Sota-san, please go ahead and take a bath.

279
00:11:37,267 --> 00:11:38,467
No, I can go last.

280
00:11:38,567 --> 00:11:40,833
Of course the guest goes first.

281
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:41,767
I'm not a guest.

282
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,900
Don't be polite. Come on, go ahead.

283
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,633
But...

284
00:11:44,733 --> 00:11:46,867
Or how about Natsuki joins you?

285
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:47,967
What?

286
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:53,067
Oh stop, I'm just kidding!

287
00:11:55,267 --> 00:11:56,267
Honestly.

288
00:12:12,633 --> 00:12:15,733
I gotta say... this is pretty nice.

289
00:12:17,967 --> 00:12:19,667
Am I sleeping on the bed?

290
00:12:20,067 --> 00:12:22,100
Or on the floor?

291
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,800
Wait, which one is it?

292
00:12:26,233 --> 00:12:29,767
Natsuki, it's your turn for the bath.

293
00:12:33,867 --> 00:12:35,467
Either way,

294
00:12:35,767 --> 00:12:36,767
it's so close.

295
00:12:37,767 --> 00:12:39,367
Natsuki?

296
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:40,833
Coming!

297
00:12:45,067 --> 00:12:46,733
Oh, Na-chan.

298
00:12:46,833 --> 00:12:47,867
Yeah.

299
00:12:47,967 --> 00:12:49,533
I borrowed some of your clothes.

300
00:12:49,633 --> 00:12:51,267
Oh, go... go right ahead.

301
00:12:51,367 --> 00:12:55,000
It felt so good to stretch
my legs out in the bath.

302
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:56,700
I'm glad.

303
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:59,200
Is that the brush you use for Rock?

304
00:12:59,667 --> 00:13:00,667
Huh?

305
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:02,200
Is that Rock's brush?

306
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:02,667
Yeah.

307
00:13:02,767 --> 00:13:05,433
Okay, hurry up and put your clothes on.

308
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,733
I need to calm down.

309
00:13:22,033 --> 00:13:24,567
You've gotten so close to Rock already.

310
00:13:44,767 --> 00:13:46,133
So cute.

311
00:13:47,367 --> 00:13:49,267
No, when I said cute,

312
00:13:49,367 --> 00:13:51,300
I meant Rock.

313
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,133
Huh.

314
00:13:56,233 --> 00:13:57,633
Did I fall asleep?

315
00:13:57,733 --> 00:14:00,033
Yeah, you did.

316
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,867
Seriously?

317
00:14:03,167 --> 00:14:06,367
Well, Rock is really soft to pet.

318
00:14:07,233 --> 00:14:09,167
Rock, this is all your fault.

319
00:14:11,967 --> 00:14:13,967
You've really come to like dogs.

320
00:14:14,067 --> 00:14:17,267
Yeah, but probably only Rock.

321
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,833
I still can't handle other dogs.

322
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,267
I see.

323
00:14:26,033 --> 00:14:27,900
The rain stopped.

324
00:14:29,867 --> 00:14:32,367
Yeah, finally.

325
00:14:32,967 --> 00:14:35,567
But you can't see any stars.

326
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:39,800
Yeah, a starless night sky.

327
00:14:40,267 --> 00:14:42,267
Doesn't it make you feel a little restless?

328
00:14:43,067 --> 00:14:44,667
Huh?

329
00:14:44,767 --> 00:14:45,933
I think it's fine.

330
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,267
I see.

331
00:14:48,367 --> 00:14:51,333
Yeah, it just makes me think
the weather won't be great tomorrow.

332
00:14:51,433 --> 00:14:54,433
Well, you always look at the sky
from a weather geek's perspective, Na-chan.

333
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:55,800
Yeah.

334
00:14:56,133 --> 00:14:58,300
It's just dark out.

335
00:14:58,400 --> 00:15:03,667
But I really like this feeling.

336
00:15:04,567 --> 00:15:06,067
Oh, really?

337
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:10,200
This isn't "love."

338
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:12,867
Definitely not.

339
00:15:25,933 --> 00:15:27,533
Na-chan.

340
00:15:29,633 --> 00:15:31,000
Yeah?

341
00:15:32,233 --> 00:15:33,833
Are you still awake?

342
00:15:36,633 --> 00:15:38,200
I'm awake.

343
00:15:40,533 --> 00:15:42,200
I knew it.

344
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,333
Can't sleep?

345
00:15:53,733 --> 00:15:55,000
Yeah.

346
00:15:56,100 --> 00:16:02,333
I feel like
I've become a part of this family,

347
00:16:02,433 --> 00:16:04,600
so I'm a little too excited.

348
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:07,667
Why are you excited?

349
00:16:11,567 --> 00:16:19,567
I'm jealous. I keep thinking,
so this is what a family feels like.

350
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:26,967
Isn't your family like this, So-chan?

351
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:33,067
Mind if I tell a late-night story?

352
00:16:35,033 --> 00:16:42,233
My family is pretty prominent
in our local area.

353
00:16:42,333 --> 00:16:43,900
But it's just a rural town.

354
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,100
Right.

355
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:48,267
No matter what we did,
people paid attention.

356
00:16:51,067 --> 00:16:54,433
Even the smallest things
would spread quickly.

357
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:57,467
So we were always worried
about what others thought.

358
00:17:00,733 --> 00:17:02,533
That sounds exhausting.

359
00:17:02,633 --> 00:17:04,567
Even at home,

360
00:17:06,433 --> 00:17:09,767
my dad was incredibly strict.

361
00:17:11,967 --> 00:17:16,700
My mom, my brother, and I were
all terrified of making him mad.

362
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:20,800
We were always walking on eggshells.

363
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:25,700
I couldn't stand that
oppressive atmosphere.

364
00:17:26,733 --> 00:17:28,667
Whenever I felt like I
was at my breaking point,

365
00:17:28,767 --> 00:17:33,067
I'd go look at a big bridge nearby.

366
00:17:33,167 --> 00:17:37,367
That bridge led to the big town next door.

367
00:17:37,467 --> 00:17:39,867
I always fantasized that if
I just crossed that bridge,

368
00:17:39,967 --> 00:17:43,833
a world of freedom would be waiting for me.

369
00:17:45,167 --> 00:17:48,567
Did you never cross it?

370
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:51,067
That bridge was only for cars.

371
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:55,133
So every time I crossed it, I
had to be with my parents.

372
00:17:58,567 --> 00:18:01,400
In the end, I still wasn't free.

373
00:18:02,467 --> 00:18:06,433
So, I always dreamed

374
00:18:07,733 --> 00:18:11,733
that one day, I'd be able
to cross to the other side

375
00:18:11,819 --> 00:18:13,853
with my own power.

376
00:18:14,433 --> 00:18:18,867
Is that where your
love for bridges started?

377
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:21,533
Maybe.

378
00:18:21,633 --> 00:18:23,067
I see.

379
00:18:24,833 --> 00:18:25,833
(Hakone Kumoyado)

380
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:34,667
What's up? You're in a great mood.

381
00:18:35,467 --> 00:18:41,467
Sota-san said he wants to
make breakfast with me tomorrow.

382
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,367
Is that so?

383
00:18:43,467 --> 00:18:46,767
Whenever I ask Rio or Natsuki to help,
they always look so reluctant.

384
00:18:46,867 --> 00:18:48,667
So I'm really happy about it.

385
00:18:49,633 --> 00:18:51,300
Fair enough.

386
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:54,600
He really is a fine young man.

387
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:59,933
So you've been playing the role
of a good young man this whole time?

388
00:19:00,167 --> 00:19:01,167
Yeah.

389
00:19:02,167 --> 00:19:05,033
What everyone expected me to be

390
00:19:06,533 --> 00:19:09,567
was a flawless, upstanding young man.

391
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:14,000
I figured if that was the case,

392
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:17,333
I might as well just play the role
of the "good young man."

393
00:19:17,433 --> 00:19:20,167
I thought it might make
things easier for me.

394
00:19:20,967 --> 00:19:22,567
That sounds even more exhausting.

395
00:19:22,667 --> 00:19:24,000
No.

396
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:30,467
Actually, it was the exact
opposite. It was a lot easier.

397
00:19:31,167 --> 00:19:32,200
Really?

398
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:33,567
Yeah.

399
00:19:34,733 --> 00:19:39,100
Even when something pissed me off,

400
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:42,300
as long as I thought,
"I'm playing the good young man right now,"

401
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,433
I could get through it.

402
00:19:45,933 --> 00:19:48,667
Is that why you're always so cheerful?

403
00:19:48,767 --> 00:19:50,000
Huh?

404
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:53,067
I'm not acting anymore.

405
00:19:53,167 --> 00:19:54,500
What?

406
00:19:55,733 --> 00:19:57,000
As I kept playing the part,

407
00:19:57,833 --> 00:19:58,967
that character...

408
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:02,900
I've become my true self.

409
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:06,500
What do you mean?

410
00:20:08,733 --> 00:20:10,333
Hard to wrap your head around, right?

411
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,600
Yeah.

412
00:20:13,167 --> 00:20:19,200
Because Na-chan and Rio are so genuine,

413
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:21,067
neither of you hide who you really are.

414
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:27,133
Is that true?

415
00:20:27,233 --> 00:20:28,433
Yeah.

416
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:36,700
Truth is, I've never had
much self-confidence.

417
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:41,267
So without realizing it,
I'd act a certain way here,

418
00:20:41,367 --> 00:20:44,733
and a completely different way there.

419
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:47,067
I'd split myself into different versions.

420
00:20:50,433 --> 00:20:54,767
But both of them are
the real So-chan, right?

421
00:20:54,867 --> 00:20:56,167
Yeah.

422
00:20:59,367 --> 00:21:04,100
Don't you ever want to just be
your unfiltered self around someone?

423
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:10,433
Probably not.

424
00:21:14,833 --> 00:21:16,633
Not even with my sister?

425
00:21:18,167 --> 00:21:19,633
Yeah.

426
00:21:24,233 --> 00:21:25,800
I see.

427
00:21:29,067 --> 00:21:34,700
But now, when I'm with Na-chan,
my true self just comes out.

428
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,367
I wonder why that is.

429
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:48,367
Maybe it's because when I'm with Na-chan,
I can finally just be me.

430
00:22:08,233 --> 00:22:09,367
Huh?

431
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:15,267
Good morning.

432
00:22:16,033 --> 00:22:17,300
Good morning.

433
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:20,800
Right.

434
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:25,833
I said too much yesterday.

435
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:30,000
No, not at all.

436
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:33,033
That's a secret just between us.

437
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:35,920
I wasn't planning on telling anyone anyway.

438
00:22:35,967 --> 00:22:37,500
Pinky promise.

439
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:39,800
We're not kids anymore.

440
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:41,233
Come on.

441
00:22:47,467 --> 00:22:48,667
It's a promise.

442
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,400
Got it.

443
00:22:56,467 --> 00:22:59,467
Sota-san, I'm back with the mint.

444
00:22:59,567 --> 00:23:00,933
Thanks.

445
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:02,700
Oh, good morning, Na-chan.

446
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:04,100
Good morning.

447
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,567
Looks great.

448
00:23:05,667 --> 00:23:08,333
- Really?
- Yeah, you're a natural.

449
00:23:08,433 --> 00:23:09,833
No way.

450
00:23:09,933 --> 00:23:16,300
This isn't love. It definitely isn't.

451
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:18,400
Probably.

452
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:19,333
Definitely.

453
00:23:19,433 --> 00:23:21,600
(This is a work of fiction)

454
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:22,867
(Next Episode)
A cold?

455
00:23:22,967 --> 00:23:24,209
(Sota's crisis shakes Na-chan's heart)
Are you okay?

456
00:23:24,233 --> 00:23:25,233
So-chan.

457
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:26,633
I heard there's someone you like?

458
00:23:26,733 --> 00:23:27,433
Here.

459
00:23:27,533 --> 00:23:30,609
(A cooking class date heats things up?) Watching
hot guys be all lovey-dovey is so therapeutic.

460
00:23:30,633 --> 00:23:33,000
I just realized he's such a worrier.

461
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:36,567
(Tears reveal true feelings)
Does this mean I really like him?
